  "context": "Step of the corpus rule remediation plan (crr-00-corpus-rule-remediation-plan). Plan written 2026-11-22 and reviewed twice by an independent adversarial reviewer; counts marked (R) were measured by that reviewer and must be re-measured, not trusted. Owner decisions were given by choice dialog on 2026-11-22 and are quoted in crr-00.",
  "description": "## Problem\nNo single function decides class, admission, lane, score source and label (T2, T3).\n\n## Change\n- One module (stdlib only, so the mirror branch can run it) that takes facts read from a result file and returns: class, public admission, maintainer admission, lane, score source, labels. Facts: benchmark, scale band from the scale registry, phases that ran, executed stream count from stream results, refresh evidence, gateway routing, known defects, validation status.\n- Generate here the stdlib-only data file of standard scales and stream minima (from the scale registry and tpc_spec.py), with a CI check that fails when it drifts. Add the rule module and the data file to the three path lists in sync-results-data-to-published.yml and to the slim-branch ADR's file list, so every later change to a mirrored file reaches published-results together with what it imports.\n- A test that enumerates every combination of the inputs (including refresh without throughput and no timed phase) and fails if one has no outcome.\n- Extend results-data/compliance-classes.json and scripts/corpus_compliance_snapshot.py (#4410) to record, for every stored result, the full outcome plus identity, score (rounded) and rank, both \"today\" (current readers) and \"rule\". No reader is moved in this item.\n- A report, attached to the pull request, of every stored result whose rule outcome differs from today's.\n\n## Decision gates\n- The reviewer measured 19 results becoming ranked (TPC-H SF1 1 to 4 platforms, TPC-DS SF1 4 to 7, TPC-DS SF10 3 to 5) and none losing rank. If the measured diff shows any result losing rank, or more than 25 becoming ranked, stop and report before crr-a2 starts.\n- Every stored result, median files included, is classified from the facts it records. The rule returns \"undetermined\" only when a needed fact is missing from the file, and the report lists each such result. Do not guess a missing fact.\n\n## Guardrails (apply to every item of this plan)\n- Fix the root cause for every platform and benchmark. No rule, exception, label or test may name a platform or a version matrix. Only the pvm-p* items may name Polars, and only to run and stage that run's files.\n- Never edit a stored result file to make it pass. Outcomes change only through the rule.\n- Any change to the outcome of a stored result must show in the committed outcome snapshot diff in the same pull request and be explained in its body.\n- No new stored class value. No reader may decide anything from benchmark.compliance_class, conformance_class or summary.tpc_metrics.suppressed.\n- Paths, line numbers and counts in this plan were read on 2026-11-22 at develop 93f3360. Re-read before editing; report drift, do not guess.\n- AGENTS.md applies: linked worktree, one pull request per item, close at the merged pull request, heavy work only through make heavy-run, no live cloud run without owner approval in that task.\n- At a decision gate, follow the recorded default. If its stop condition is met, stop and report to the owner. Never substitute a different owner decision.\n- Read crr-00-corpus-rule-remediation-plan first: it holds the owner decisions, the rule table and the fault types (T1 to T5).",
